{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"trainsick-fleeting-avocet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nFollow-up to winning-endurant-xenops. Before the fold defer-guard lands, any fold that crossed an un-cited pre-snapshot orphan LAUNDERED it: the event file was retired and its uuid cited in source_event_uuids without its effect entering the compiled state. fsck reports clean on such tickets. The data is NOT lost — retired files are preserved and rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log replays the full log including .retired — but there is no DETECTION: finding historical laundering requires comparing each ticket's snapshot-compiled state against a full-log replay (expensive, so an opt-in deep check, e.g. fsck --deep or --verify-snapshots).\n## Proposed direction\nOpt-in fsck deep verification: for each ticket with a snapshot, replay full log (incl .retired) and diff against snapshot-compiled state; mismatch => LAUNDERED_SNAPSHOT finding routed to the existing rebuild door. Known live incidents: one (e27c orphan, healed pre-fold) — historical damage believed bounded.\n## Out of scope\nThe forward-path defer guard (xenops).","id":"2aaf-90b9-4a31-43bf","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"fsck deep check: detect historically laundered snapshots (cited-but-effect-missing)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786726455618236001,"uuid":"44a9808e-91b8-4bee-91f1-f178b8b80048"}